# a function defined of a type, bracket-less (wiki/function.md): `square of number = it * it` is `square(it: number) := it * it`

'square of number = it * it; square 3'	9
'square of a number = it * it; square(3)'	9
'foo of any = 1; foo(3)'	1
'foo of int = it+it; foo of text = it.length; foo of any = 1; foo("abc") + foo(2) + foo(2.5)'	8
'p = {name: "Bo"}; name of p'	"Bo"
# := spells the of form too (decision of-form-canonical); a preposition or pronoun in a head is never a parameter (wiki/matching.md)
'double of int := it * 2; double 3'	6
'double of an int := it * 2; double(3)'	6
'canvas = {width: 1}; width of canvas := 12; canvas'	{width: 12}
# a pronoun in a spaced definition head is no parameter: the definition reads it as the argument
'twice it := it * 2; twice 3'	6
